The fuzzer takes raw bytes as Ruby code. So the PoC is a Ruby source code string. The vulnerability is in `mrb_ary_splice` -> `value_move` doing an out-of-bounds read.

Let me understand the vulnerability better. The issue is in `mrb_ary_splice` at line 804:
```c
value_move(ptr + head + argc, ptr + tail, alen - tail);
```

Let me think about the conditions. The `value_move` function:
```c
static inline void
value_move(mrb_value *s1, const mrb_value *s2, size_t n)
{
  if (n == 0) return;
  if (s1 > s2 && s1 < s2 + n)  // overlapping forward
  {
    s1 += n;
    s2 += n;
    while (n-- > 0) {
      *--s1 = *--s2;
    }
  }
  else if (s1 != s2) {
    while (n-- > 0) {
      *s1++ = *s2++;
    }
  }
  ...
}
```

The OOB read happens "8 bytes past a heap-allocated array". Let me think about how this can happen.

